==Strategy==
This stage pairs Deathkory and Ackey, a deadly duo. The two heavily limit the usage of cats, but luckily, Ackey is only at 100% here, meaning he doesn't deal too much damage and can be taken care of with a well-timed [[Ancient Egg: N109 (Rare Cat)|Barrel Cat]] or two. The money here is relatively tight, but manageable due to the consistency of Croconators and Sir Seals, which should give enough money. The stage begins with a Croconator and Deathkory, use [[Aku Researcher (Rare Cat)|Aku Researcher]] to take out the Croconator and, with luck, break Deathkorys [[Shield]]. Use [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Octopus Cat]] to block Deathkorys waves and allow for attackers like [[Nymph Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fiend Cat]], [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] or [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman Cat]]. Any meatshields will work well, especially fast, Wave immune, or [[Immune to Freeze|Freeze Immune]] meatshields such as [[Maize Cat (Rare Cat)|Cone Cat]], [[Carpenter Cat (Rare Cat)|Rapper Cat]], or [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Eraser Cat]]. The former two work very well due to their abilities/immunities respectively, but are hard to obtain.

=== '''Recommended Ubers''' ===

* [[Yaminora]]: Serves as an Anti-Aku Weakener for both Ackey and Deathkory, and in True Form can also act as a Wave Shield that can replace Octopus Cat. True Form is basically mandatory to gain the Wave Shield ability which blocks Deathkory's Waves. Also has a really good "Resistant up" M [[Dark End to the Holiday (Combo)|Combo]] with [[Tourist Cat]] that can help both Yaminora and Cone Cat (even Barrel Cat but the effects are negligible) if you have him, which can help them tank/survive longer.

